The repository only tracks a single `HARNESS` file — the Android project code is untracked in the working tree (as expected for this harness setup). My fix is on disk and the build succeeded.

## Bug Fix Summary

**Bug:** Robotic Arm shows a rounded/truncated value instead of the exact value entered via keyboard. Entering "38" displayed "36" due to integer truncation in `degree / 3.6` (38/3.6 = 10.55 → 10, and 10×3.6 = 36).

**File modified:** `app/src/main/java/io/pslab/activity/RoboticArmActivity.java`

**Change in `processDegreeInput()` method:**

```diff
         } else {
             seekArc.setProgress((int) (degree / 3.6));
             editEnter = true;
+            degreeText.setText(degreeStr);
         }
```

**Why this works:** The SeekArc uses a 0-100 scale where progress is converted to degrees via `progress × 3.6`. This creates a many-to-one mapping — multiple degree values round to the same SeekArc progress. The `onProgressChanged` callback (which displays `progress × 3.6`) may not fire when progress doesn't change, or may show a different value if it does. By directly setting `degreeText` to the exact string the user typed, we guarantee the displayed value always matches the user's input.

**Verification:** `./gradlew clean assembleDebug` completed successfully with no errors.

